is retained in LICENSES/bb-zcode-MIT.txt.

Local changes replace the runtime schema dependency with narrow local validators,
use this adapter's workspace identity and support an explicit Desktop storage
root. The login reader also permits JWT-only Start sign-in and independent plan
discovery without filtering by Desktop's currently selected connection.
The module's build-native-auth.mjs produces the runtime from its reference
source; the plugin build command delegates to it. ACP, account and quota runtime
implementations now belong to zcode-acp. The plugin retains BB integration and
the original GUI bridge. The host bundle includes the module's MIT account code,
so the full attribution is also retained with this plugin's distribution.
